<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-code-traceability-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series — Code-to-model traceability: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every model function cites the page / equation it implements (E1-E6), Thompson's tables are constants with page comments, and the Lean file names the theorem for each law. Docked because the analysis-side choices (PCA frame from the mid-ontogeny outline, 0.85 scale-break threshold, 5-95 % interior trimming, thresholds in T1-T4) are documented in comments but not tied to any source or pre-registration beyond the scout manifest's generic T1-T4 list." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py L215–L229: specimen_axis_dims: PCA frame choice justified in docstring but not sourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L215-L229>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-code-traceability-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-model-fidelity-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E1-E5 are implemented exactly as Thompson states them and verified numerically against the Lean theorems in self_test; the generative model (E6) is Thompson's verbal construction made explicit and its limiting cases (d = 0 Nodosarian, rho = 1 Orbitolitid) are correct. Docked because chamber radius a0 and overlap are unconstrained free choices with no source value, the Textularian translation T is implemented but never exercised or shown, and the Raup (1966) W-D-T correspondence is asserted in a docstring rather than demonstrated." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py L109–L127: a0 = 0.6 default and translation parameter have no source value; T is never used in any figure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L109-L127>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-morphometric-validation-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series — Morphometric validation: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Strong core: 106 specimens x ~13 stages, per-specimen r / RMSE / ratio CV / BIC vs arithmetic, genus means with SD, and an explicit comparison with Thompson's printed 1.225 and 1.5 (T3 passes at 1.239 / 1.53). Thompson's own tables are refitted and his stated ratios recovered. Docked because: no confidence intervals or KS/normality test on residuals; T2 (CV <= 0.15) cannot detect the systematic ontogenetic hump of the pseudoschwagerines seen in panel G; T4 uses an uncalibrated threshold whose null expectation (~6.6 for n ~ 96) exceeds the cut-off, so the v1 FAIL is an artefact of the statistic, not of the data; no negative control." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py L309–L339: verdict_from_metrics: T1-T4 rules; T2 is CV-only, T4 threshold 6.0 is arbitrary <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L309-L339>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-measurement-fraction-of-specimens-where-geometric-beats-arithmetic-growth-bic>,
