<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-overall-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series — MorphoEval overall 62.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "v1 implements Thompson's model faithfully as far as he states it (constant ratio, constant angle, limiting cases, mass-proportional volume law) and tests the central quantitative claim on a correctly matched public dataset: 106 fusulinid specimens give median r = 0.995 for ln D vs half-whorl stage, the geometric law beats arithmetic growth in 100 % of specimens, and Triticites reproduces von Moller's Fusulina ratio (1.239 +/- 0.021 vs 1.225 per half-whorl; 1.53 vs 1.5 per whorl). Weaknesses: (1) the real specimen photograph is shown but not segmented or measured, so specimen-match rests on eyeballing; (2) no parameter sweep demonstrates that W, d, overlap and T control the model's form monotonically — the four morphs are hand-picked points; (3) no negative control (shuffled stages / synthetic arithmetic series / random-walk ratios) is run through the verdict rules; (4) the panel-G finding that pseudoschwagerine ratios rise to ~1.45 and fall to ~1.1 through ontogeny (systematic, not a 'small secondary fluctuation') is visible but untested — T2 uses only a CV threshold, so the verdict machinery cannot register the most interesting deviation from Thompson's law; (5) T4 threshold is uncalibrated (for n ~ 96 interior points the expected max/median gap of a continuous distribution is ~6.6, so 6.34 is the null expectation); (6) goodness-of-fit lacks KS/normality of residuals and confidence intervals; (7) the GIF model shell uses an arbitrary a0 = 0.5 that does not resemble Nummulina; (8) environment versions differ from requirements.lock.txt. Overall 62.5/100 (faithfulness 57.1, reproducibility 75.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1, lean 4.35.0, lockfile requirements.lock.txt (NOT the versions used here — pip resolved newer numpy/matplotlib/Pillow). Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 45, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 62, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 70, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py at 0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4, image/png, 557632 B, 1760×1100 px, artifact_sha256 3ac36d67d48be41b7dd503a4b25e70dd907fd2b4e7d04fb54b22ffa833f905ba (sha256 3ac36d67d48be41b7dd503a4b25e70dd907fd2b4e7d04fb54b22ffa833f905ba), spec_fingerprint e8dfa9fdde138927298f774fce032da52edc892f40295eed80203fdda26888b1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e8dfa9fdde138927298f774fce032da52edc892f40295eed80203fdda26888b1; artifact_sha256: 3ac36d67d48be41b7dd503a4b25e70dd907fd2b4e7d04fb54b22ffa833f905ba; input_dataset_sha256: {fusulinid_axial_thin_section_commons_NEON.jpg=39f54718bbc8afa2..., shi2020_dryad_sn02v6x26_Landmarks.dat=f7bb3fe73332d58c..., shi2020_dryad_sn02v6x26_Table_1.csv=b5ddc6561b74b26d..., t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif=71030d8c3199fbae..., thompson1917_fig309_nummulina_antiquior_vonmoller_p591.jpg=e7e37b2c3ea0a6f3...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 591-598: chambers/whorls in continued proportion lie on a logarithmic spiral; von Moller's Fusulina whorls in ratio ~1.5 (half-whorl 1.225, alpha ~86 deg); van Iterson's Triloculina 1.323; Rhumbler's Pulvinulina ~1.187 with a 'small secondary fluctuation'; constant volume ratio from growth proportional to existing mass. | Thompson (1917) pp. 602-605: rotaline, Miliolid, Nodosarian, Textularian, Orbitolitid forms are all logarithmic-spiral cases differing in numerical coefficients and pass into one another by continuous gradations.; reconstructed_in_script: A discrete similar-chamber generative model (centres on r = r0 rho^k at angle k d, radii a0 rho^k, optional translation) that Thompson describes verbally; chamber size a0 and overlap are free choices, not source parameters. | Per-specimen log-linear fits of test DIAMETER (perpendicular to the coiling axis, PCA frame from the mid-ontogeny outline) vs half-whorl stage on the Dryad outlines; BIC comparison with linear growth; CV and linear trend of successive ratios; a gap/overlap statistic for genus continuity; pre-registered pass/fail thresholds (r >= 0.98, 80 %, CV <= 0.15, +/-0.05, gap ratio <= 6). | Longest-segment rule for the 14 specimens digitised at two magnifications.; transfer_boundary: Dryad outlines are whorl-level axial sections in pixels of Late Paleozoic fusulinids; Thompson's chamber-level claims (septal chambers, Miliolidae, rotaline forms) are tested only via his own printed tables and the generative model, not via new specimen measurements. | The fusulinid thin-section photograph is displayed but not measured in v1.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that the growth ratio is physiologically caused by mass-proportional growth (E4 is proved algebraically, not tested). | Does not claim the verdict generalises to planktonic or miliolid foraminifera; n = 5 fusulinid genera, 106 specimens, one Dryad deposit. | The T4 'continuity' statistic is a heuristic with an arbitrary threshold; its FAIL in v1 (gap ratio 6.34 vs 6.0) is not evidence of discontinuity.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': \"specimen-match / morphometric-validation (L429-L434): segment the fusulinid thin section — locate the proloculus, take sector-median radial intensity profiles along the minor axis, detect dark whorl walls, fit ln r_j vs j, and compare the resulting whorl ratio with the Dryad Triticites and Thompson's 1.5; overlay detected walls on panel E.\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'parameter-expressivity (L367-L377): add a (W, d) sweep of the generative model with morphometric read-outs (chambers per whorl, chamber overlap fraction, coiling tightness r_last/r_first, aspect ratio) and show monotonic control; exercise the translation T (Textularian) branch.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'morphometric-validation (L309-L339): add a negative/ablation control — run the verdict rules on (a) within-specimen shuffled stage order, (b) synthetic arithmetic-growth series with matched noise, (c) random-walk ratios — and report that T1/T3 reject them.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'morphometric-validation (L318): replace the CV-only T2 with a test of systematic ratio drift (quadratic term in ln D vs k with its t-statistic / p-value per genus, plus the stage of maximum ratio) so the pseudoschwagerine inflation hump in panel G is scored, not just plotted.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'morphometric-validation (L329): calibrate T4 with a Monte-Carlo null — the largest interior gap of n samples from a continuous (normal / KDE) fit to the pooled ratios — and report a p-value instead of the fixed 6.0 threshold.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'morphometric-validation (L143-L175): add goodness-of-fit statistics — KS test of log residuals against normal, bootstrap 95 % CI of the genus mean ratios, RMSE in both spaces — and expose them in measure_morphoeval().'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': \"specimen-match (L491): choose GIF/figure model parameters from the data (W from the Triticites fit, d and a0 fitted to Fig. 309's visible chamber count per whorl) and draw the model section next to the Fig. 309 crop.\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': 'repro-package (L644-L688): stamp numpy/matplotlib/Pillow versions and the script version into the metrics JSON; add headline-number regression assertions to --self-test; drop the unused scipy mention from the README environment list or use scipy for the KS test.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R9', 'item': 'source-traceability (paper_citations.bib L12-L40): add resolvable URLs (BHL / IA) for von Moller 1878 and van Iterson 1907, and a DOI or URL for Przibram 1913.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.25e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-parameter-expressivity-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series — Parameter expressivity: 50/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Only four hand-picked (W, d, a0) points are rendered; there is no sweep across W or d, no morphometric read-out (coiling tightness, chamber overlap fraction, number of chambers per whorl, aspect ratio) as a function of parameter, and so monotonic control is asserted (and proven in Lean for size) but not shown for form. The Nodosarian branch of chamber_series is exercised only in self_test." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
