<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-specimen-match-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series — Morphological realism / specimen match: 45/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Panel A's four morphs are recognisably Globigerina-like, Cyclammina-like (Fig. 313 style 20-degree chambers), Triloculina-like and an Orbitolitid ring, and are visually distinct from one another (credited). Panel E shows a genuine fusulinid axial section next to panel F's Dryad outlines, and the two are the same kind of object (fusiform nested whorls). But nothing is overlaid or measured on the photograph, the model shells are never compared with Fig. 309 Nummulina or with the thin section, and the GIF's 'Nummulina-like' shell (a0 = 0.5, d = 24 degrees) is a thick ring of overlapping discs that does not resemble either specimen image." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py L429–L434: specimen image only imshow'd — no segmentation, no whorl-wall detection, no model overlay <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L429-L434>",
        "thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py L491–L491: GIF model shell chamber_series(30, W, 24.0, r0=1.0, a0=0.5): arbitrary a0, visually unlike Nummulina (Fig. 309) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L491-L491>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-specimen-match-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

