<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-029-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Continued-Proportion Chamber Succession & Gnomonic Self-Similarity Law" ;
    dct:description "Formalises the core of claim T1917-029: a constant ratio makes every later chamber a gnomon of the earlier shell (p. 591 'the big many-chambered shell is of just the same shape as the smaller and younger shell'), gives the half-whorl -> whorl rule used on p. 593, and yields the index-free cross-product invariance tested on the Dryad fusulinid half-whorl series | Variables: L_n: linear breadth of chamber or half-whorl n; L_1: initial breadth; ρ: constant linear growth ratio (1.187 Pulvinulina, 1.225 Fusulina half-whorl, 1.323 Triloculina); W = ρ_half²: whole-whorl ratio (1.5 Fusulina)" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form, Ch. XII pp. 591-595 (von Moller Fusulina table p. 593; van Iterson Triloculina table p. 595)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean#L61-L83>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L120-L175> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def chamberSize (L1 rho n : Nat) : Nat :=
  L1 * rho ^ n
theorem geometric_succession_is_gnomonic (L1 rho n m : Nat) :
    chamberSize L1 rho (n + 1) = rho * chamberSize L1 rho n ∧
    chamberSize L1 rho (n + m) = rho ^ m * chamberSize L1 rho n ∧
    chamberSize L1 rho (n + 2) = (rho * rho) * chamberSize L1 rho n ∧
    chamberSize L1 rho (n + 1) * chamberSize L1 rho m
      = chamberSize L1 rho n * chamberSize L1 rho (m + 1)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L_n = L_1 ρ^n,   L_{n+1}/L_n = ρ,   L_{n+m} = ρ^m L_n,   W = ρ_half^2,   L_{n+1} L_m = L_n L_{m+1}" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2020.53>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sn02v6x26> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Logarithmic-Spiral Chamber Succession & Gnomonic Geometric Growth (Thompson 1917 Ch. XII, quantitative-geometric)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.chamberSize" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.geometric_succession_is_gnomonic" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-029-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Mass-Proportional Growth => Constant Chamber-Volume Ratio Law" ;
    dct:description "Thompson's physiological derivation (pp. 597-598) of why the ratio should be constant: growth at each instant proportional to the whole existing mass; the Lean proof shows the recursion closes to a geometric series exactly | Variables: V_n: volume of chamber n; S_n: cumulative shell mass; q: growth increment as a fraction of the whole pre-existing mass; 1+q: constant volume ratio; ρ = (1+q)^{1/3} for similar chambers" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form, Ch. XII pp. 597-598" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean#L89-L113>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L176-L200> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cumMass (V0 q : Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => V0
  | n + 1 => (1 + q) * cumMass V0 q n
def chamberVol (V0 q n : Nat) : Nat :=
  q * cumMass V0 q n
theorem thompson_mass_proportional_growth_constant_volume_ratio (V0 q n : Nat) :
    chamberVol V0 q (n + 1) = (1 + q) * chamberVol V0 q n ∧
    cumMass V0 q n = V0 * (1 + q) ^ n ∧
    chamberVol V0 q n = q * V0 * (1 + q) ^ n
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "V_{n+1} = q (V_0 + V_1 + ... + V_n)   ⟹   V_{n+2}/V_{n+1} = 1 + q,   S_n = V_0 (1+q)^n,   V_{n+1} = q V_0 (1+q)^n" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2020.53>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sn02v6x26> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Logarithmic-Spiral Chamber Succession & Gnomonic Geometric Growth (Thompson 1917 Ch. XII, quantitative-geometric)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.chamberVol" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.thompson_mass_proportional_growth_constant_volume_ratio" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-029-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "von Moller / Thompson (1917) Log-Difference Constancy: Half-Whorl 0.088 -> Whole-Whorl 0.176 (log10 1.5)" ;
    dct:description "Makes the p. 593 arithmetic a theorem: a linear log-size series has constant first differences and doubled alternate differences, which is exactly the statistic (slope of log D_k on half-whorl index k) fitted per specimen on the Dryad data | Variables: a: log of the first half-whorl breadth (von Moller 0.982 for 0.096 mm); c: constant log-difference per half-whorl (0.088); 2c: per whorl (0.176)" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form, Ch. XII p. 593 (von Moller 1878 Fusulina cylindrica opposite-whorl series)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean#L119-L134>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L300-L360> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def logSize (a c n : Nat) : Nat :=
  a + n * c
theorem log_difference_constancy_half_and_whole_whorl (a c n : Nat) :
    logSize a c (n + 1) - logSize a c n = c ∧
    logSize a c (n + 2) - logSize a c n = 2 * c ∧
    logSize 982 88 2 - logSize 982 88 0 = 176
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "log L_n = a + n c;   log L_{n+1} − log L_n = c;   log L_{n+2} − log L_n = 2c;   c = 0.088 ⟹ 2c = 0.176 = log10 1.5" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2020.53>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sn02v6x26> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Logarithmic-Spiral Chamber Succession & Gnomonic Geometric Growth (Thompson 1917 Ch. XII, quantitative-geometric)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.logSize" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.log_difference_constancy_half_and_whole_whorl" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-029-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Equal-Angle Condition & Whorl Periodicity (Biloculina 180°, Triloculina 120°, Cyclammina 20°)" ;
    dct:description "The second of Thompson's two conditions for a logarithmic spiral (pp. 595-597): with equal subtended angles the geometric series of chambers closes into whorls with ratio W = ρ^m; drives the generative chamber model's Miliolid, Cyclammina and rotaline morphs | Variables: θ_n: vectorial angle of chamber n (degrees); d: constant angle subtended by one chamber; m: chambers per whorl; ρ^m = W: whorl ratio" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form, Ch. XII pp. 595-597, Figs. 311-313" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean#L140-L155>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L120-L175> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def chamberAngle (d n : Nat) : Nat :=
  n * d
theorem equal_angle_whorl_periodicity (d m n L1 rho : Nat) (h : m * d = 360) :
    chamberAngle d (n + m) = chamberAngle d n + 360 ∧
    chamberSize L1 rho (n + m) = rho ^ m * chamberSize L1 rho n ∧
    chamberAngle 180 2 = 360 ∧ chamberAngle 120 3 = 360 ∧ chamberAngle 20 18 = 360
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "θ_n = n d;   m d = 360 ⟹ θ_{n+m} = θ_n + 360 ∧ L_{n+m} = ρ^m L_n;   (d, m) ∈ {(180, 2), (120, 3), (20, 18)}" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2020.53>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sn02v6x26> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Logarithmic-Spiral Chamber Succession & Gnomonic Geometric Growth (Thompson 1917 Ch. XII, quantitative-geometric)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.chamberAngle" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.equal_angle_whorl_periodicity" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-029-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Continuous Series of Genera: Monotone Ratio Ordering with Orbitolitid (ρ = 1) and Nodosarian (d = 0) Limits" ;
    dct:description "Formal content of the 'continuous geometric series transformable into one another' half of the claim (pp. 602-605): the family is totally ordered along the ratio axis and contains Thompson's two limiting cases as members, not exceptions | Variables: ρ, ρ': two growth ratios (two genera); n: chamber index; d = 0: Nodosarian limiting angle; ρ = 1: Orbitolitid limiting ratio" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form, Ch. XII pp. 602-605" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean#L162-L171>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0eb517d23d79fca6826d903b09d425781dd017b4/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py#L400-L470> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem continuous_series_and_limiting_cases (L1 rho rho' n : Nat) (h : rho ≤ rho') :
    chamberSize L1 rho n ≤ chamberSize L1 rho' n ∧
    chamberSize L1 1 n = L1 ∧
    chamberAngle 0 n = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "ρ ≤ ρ' ⟹ L_1 ρ^n ≤ L_1 ρ'^n;   ρ = 1 ⟹ L_n = L_1 (circle, α = 90°);   d = 0 ⟹ θ_n = 0 (straight Nodosarian line)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2020.53>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sn02v6x26> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Logarithmic-Spiral Chamber Succession & Gnomonic Geometric Growth (Thompson 1917 Ch. XII, quantitative-geometric)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.chamberSize" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_223.continuous_series_and_limiting_cases" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

